1. Definitions.
   1.1 “Software” means the licensed work, including source code, object code, and accompanying materials.
   1.2 “You” (or “Licensee”) means any individual or legal entity exercising permissions granted by this License.
   1.3 “Small Business” means an organization that, together with all affiliates, has fewer than 25 total employees and contractors, and less than US$500,000 total revenue in the most recent 12‑month period.
   1.4 “Non‑Qualifying Entity” means any entity that is not a Small Business, including large corporations and organizations exceeding either threshold in Section 1.3.
   1.5 “As‑a‑Service” means providing third parties with access to any substantial set of the features or functionality of the Software as a hosted, managed, cloud, or similar service.
   1.6 “AI Training” means using the Software, its contents, derivatives, outputs, metadata, embeddings, or usage data to train, fine‑tune, retrain, or otherwise improve any AI, ML, LLM, diffusion, or related model, dataset, or system.
   1.7 “Usage Data” means telemetry, logs, prompts, completions, or other data arising from use of the Software by any party.

