3. Eligibility. Only individuals acting in a personal capacity and Small Businesses may exercise the License; Non‑Qualifying Entities are not granted any rights under this License.

4. Prohibited Uses.
   4.1 No AI Training. You must not engage in AI Training using the Software, any derivative works, outputs, or Usage Data, directly or indirectly, including via third parties or data brokers.
   4.2 No As‑a‑Service. You must not provide the Software, or any derivative, to third parties as an As‑a‑Service offering where users access any substantial set of its features (see ELv2’s scenario explanations) or functionality, whether paid or free.
   4.3 No Use by Non‑Qualifying Entities. Non‑Qualifying Entities must not use, copy, modify, host, or redistribute the Software for any purpose without a separate commercial license from Licensor.
   4.4 No Circumvention. You must not circumvent or assist others in circumventing these restrictions, including through proxy services or layered offerings.

5. Permitted Uses. Subject to Sections 3–4, individuals and Small Businesses may use the Software internally, create modifications, and redistribute source or binary forms to other individuals and Small Businesses, provided recipients receive this License and are eligible under Section 3.

6. Attribution. Any redistribution must include the above copyright notice and this License in full, and must not remove notices identifying the Licensor.

7. Verification. On Licensor’s written request, You will provide a written attestation of compliance (including headcount and revenue confirmation sufficient to determine Small Business status) within 30 days; no access to confidential financial records is required.

8. Termination and Cure. This License terminates automatically if You breach it and fail to cure within 30 days of notice; upon termination, all rights immediately cease, and You must stop using and distributing the Software.

